-# NFSU2 Driving Tools: experimental v0.31.0
+# NFSU2 Driving Tools: experimental v0.32.0
 
 Unpacked Chrome / Edge / Brave extension for https://nfsu2.xyz/. See `CHANGELOG.md` for this release's changes and verification limits.
 
-## v0.31.0: Keep owned Drag AI through settings refreshes
+## v0.32.0: Race-only automatic driver
+
+In **AI driver**, enable **Race-only automatic driver** to arm the native driver for races you start or join yourself. It waits for the active race/GO state, includes Street X, Drag and Drift, and requests handback in free roam, outrun, results or other ineligible contexts. It does not find, join, start, replay or vote for events.
+
+The existing **Automatic driver** still includes free roam. Selecting either driver mode turns the other off. The race-only switch is **off by default**, stays armed between races on this page, and resets on page reload or profile Load. It is deliberately not added to saved profiles; existing saved choices and storage remain unchanged.
+
+**F7, F9/Stop, or driving-key takeover during a race disarms race-only AI.** Manual steering in free roam leaves it armed. If driving controls are still physically held when entering a race, acquisition waits until they are released. Turning the switch off requests native handback. A genuine native manual request, finished/totaled state, failed-control latch or watchdog is not forced back to AI.
+
+Online races still need the existing **Allow network tools** permission. Exact build, current ownership, race, focus/menu, native driver and handback guards are retained. A selected switch is not proof of active ownership; the HUD and local log show the effective request and native observations separately.
+
+Optional **Adaptive road-race speed** is also included below. It remains off by default and leaves Street X unchanged. Neither option changes steering, shifting, NOS, game saves or native AI code. Live race efficacy and browser appearance remain unverified.
+
+**Verification:** the complete combined release passes **1,907 automated tests, zero failures/skips/cancellations**, including race-only eligibility/lifecycle, optional adaptive mode, joint Street X/online/stop behavior and all retained features. Independent tests additionally cover production native handback and cached-route reconstruction. All four supported patched game module outputs remain byte-identical to v0.31.
+
+For an existing installation, replace matching files in the already loaded extension folder, click **Reload** on that extension's browser card, then refresh the game. Verify **0.32.0**. Do not remove/re-add the extension or create a different folder just for this update.
+
+## Optional adaptive road-race speed
+
+A new **default-off, session-only** option coordinates the existing native route planner. Its separate straight-target ceiling defaults to **1.30×** and ranges from 1.00× to 2.00×. The native route uses distance to known corners to lower its target in advance while retaining a higher target on sufficiently long straights. This is a planned target factor, not a physical speed cap or a measured speed increase.
+
+Enable either **Race-only automatic driver** or **Automatic driver**, then **Adaptive road-race speed** in AI driver → Road-race settings. Online use also requires **Allow network tools**. Adaptive mode uses the existing Race corner speed, Race sharp-turn margin and Race braking factor values, even when the separate Road-race hairpin assist switch is off. Lower braking factor requests earlier braking. It overrides the effective custom race pace only in eligible ordinary road races, without changing any saved switch or slider.
+
+**Street X keeps the exact existing pace, corner and braking selections.** Adaptive mode is dormant in actual/forced Street X and the known online Street X mode. Drag, Drift/forced variants, Outrun and free roam are also excluded. Selecting adaptive mode does not turn on Automatic driver or network permission.
+
+The optional ceiling stays constant while driving. The existing native route envelope varies by distance; JavaScript does not switch pace or reconstruct the driver at every corner. A deliberate setting or race-mode change may still require the existing OFF/acknowledgement/ON route reconstruction. Manual takeover, race end, permission withdrawal and the existing watchdog remain in force.
+
+F7/manual driving keys stop AI and leave the optional selection dormant. F9/Stop, profile Load and page reload turn adaptive mode off. It is not added to saved tool profiles or legacy session preferences. Blur, hidden page and menus pause it normally. Turn it off to return to the prior controls after native handoff.
+
+The HUD and local log distinguish a request, matching native pace acknowledgement, and observed corner/braking hook evidence. These counters do not measure braking success, safe corner entry or a clean lap. There is no new steering, obstacle avoidance, NOS control, added route horizon, opponent manipulation or collision protection. Higher targets can still cause crashes. Start at 1.30× and assess one change at a time.
+
+Only page orchestration, a pure selector and bounded diagnostics change. Native hooks, the AI controller, engine tuning, NOS clock correction, Drag-retention fix, tuner and saved-profile implementation remain byte-for-byte unchanged from v0.31. Exact-native synthetic tests support the route-speed envelope; live racing, lap times, wins and browser layout remain unverified.
+
+## Retained v0.31.0: Keep owned Drag AI through settings refreshes
 
 A reproduced publication race could let the game's manual-Drag selector run while the extension refreshed the same active settings. The new guard retains an **already-owned, currently permitted native Drag AI lease** through that brief write. It does not acquire new control, force a real manual request back to AI, or change steering, shifting, NOS or damage.
 
